silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_03_full_and_faithful_embedding_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'FullAndFaithfulEmbeddingConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, ColimitFactorizationArrow_VetCarePlan: the unique arrow VetCarePlan_77 -> MittensColimitApex; the concrete fullness witness — the natural transformation Hom(-,VetCarePlan_77) -> Hom(-,MittensColimitApex) arises from exactly this arrow; also, DistinctLegArrows_D_Mittens: the twelve distinct leg arrows of D_Mittens (record_leg, identifier_leg, ..., taxonomy_leg); faithfulness means they yield twelve distinct natural transformations; no two produce the same Nat(Hom(-,X), Hom(-,MittensColimitApex)); also, VetCarePlan_77: the clinical care plan document for Mittens at Tartu Animal Clinic; a competing cocone (a cone from D_Mittens that also receives all twelve legs); the colimit factorization gives the unique arrow VetCarePlan_77 -> MittensColimitApex." .
